                    <death when="1858-12-01"/>
                    <occupation>printer</occupation>
                    <occupation>naturalist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Richard Taylor was a printer who was a fellow of a number of prestigious organizations such as the Linnean Society, the Society of
  Antiquaries, and the Philological Society. He was the son of <persName key="TAY02 TAY04">John and Susannah Taylor</persName>
   of Norwich who also appear in the diary.</p>
                        <p>'R Taylor' and 'RT' have been identified as Richard along with some instances of 'Taylor'; 
     see further discusion at <persName key="TAY01">John Taylor</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS. Abinger c. 10, fol. 5: 12 September 1806.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS. Abinger c. 10, fols. 27-8: 2 March 1807.</bibl>
